</head>
<body>

  <div class="top-stripe"></div>

  <!-- NAV -->
  <SiteNav />

  <div class="page">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <div class="hero-section">
      <div class="indictment-badge">
        <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2L15.09 8.26L22 9.27L17 14.14L18.18 21.02L12 17.77L5.82 21.02L7 14.14L2 9.27L8.91 8.26L12 2Z"/></svg>
        Prophetic Warning &mdash; Revelation 14 &amp; 18 &mdash; Your Eternal Destiny Is On The Line
      </div>
      <h1 class="hero-h1">
        The Test That<br>
        <em>Decides Your Eternal Destiny</em><br>
        <strong>Hangs on How You Obey<br>When You Learn the Truth</strong>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        The Lord has shown with crystal clarity that <strong>the image of the beast WILL BE FORMED before probation closes.</strong>
        It is <strong>THE great test</strong> for the people of God. Not a test of doctrine. Not a test of theology.
        <strong>A test of obedience when the truth costs you everything.</strong>
        The same religious persecution the Pilgrims fled on the Mayflower in 1620 is being enforced today
        &mdash; not in England, but in the incorporated state churches of America, cloaked in tax-exempt paperwork
        and the legal name <em>&ldquo;Seventh-day Adventist.&rdquo;</em>
        The Loud Cry of Revelation 18:1&ndash;4 is sounding. <strong>Will you come out? Or will you be partakers of her plagues?</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="hero-truth-pill">
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm-2 14.5v-9l6 4.5-6 4.5z"/></svg>
        Revelation 18:4 &mdash; &ldquo;Come out of her, my people&rdquo; &mdash; NOW &mdash; Before It Is Too Late
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- EGW MEGA WARNING — THE GREAT TEST -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow-red">Ellen G. White &mdash; The Clearest Warning in the Spirit of Prophecy</div>
      <h2 class="sect h2" style="font-family:'Crimson Text',serif;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.2vw,2.7rem);font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:22px;line-height:1.15;">The Image of the Beast <em>WILL BE FORMED.</em><br>Your Eternal Destiny Is Decided Here.</h2>

      <div class="mega-warn">
        <div class="mega-warn-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="36" height="36" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 001.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 001.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 00-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="mega-warn-eyebrow">Thus Saith the Lord Through His Messenger &mdash; The Gravest Possible Warning</div>
        <blockquote>
          &ldquo;The Lord has shown me clearly that <strong>the image of the beast will be formed</strong> before probation closes, for it is to be <strong>the great test</strong> for the people of God, by which <strong>their eternal destiny will be decided.</strong>&rdquo;
        </blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Ellen G. White &mdash; Manuscript 51, 1899 &mdash; Cited in Last Day Events, p. 134</cite>
      </div>

      <p class="sect-sub">
        Let that land with its full weight. <strong>Your eternal destiny</strong> &mdash; heaven or the seven last plagues, life or ruin &mdash;
        is <em>decided by this test.</em> Not by a test you take in a comfortable pew with your theology intact and your tithe records perfect.
        It is decided by what you do <strong>when the image of the beast confronts you personally</strong> &mdash; when the institution you
        trusted, the church you were baptized in, the organization you gave your life savings to, is revealed to be
        standing on the wrong side of prophetic history. The image of the beast is not coming. <em>It is already formed.</em>
        It was formed on <strong>April 15, 1904</strong> in Washington, District of Columbia.
      </p>

      <div class="mega-quote">
        <div class="mega-quote-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2L15.09 8.26L22 9.27L17 14.14L18.18 21.02L12 17.77L5.82 21.02L7 14.14L2 9.27L8.91 8.26L12 2Z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <blockquote>
          &ldquo;We cannot now step off the foundation that God has established. We cannot now enter into
          <strong>any new organization;</strong> for this would mean <strong>apostasy from the truth.</strong>
          Their foundation would be built on the sand, and storm and tempest would sweep away the structure.&rdquo;
        </blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Ellen G. White &mdash; 1 Selected Messages, p. 204 &mdash; Letter 242, 1903</cite>
      </div>

      <p class="sect-sub">
        Six months after EGW wrote these words, on April 15, 1904, five men signed a legal document in Washington D.C.
        creating the <strong>&ldquo;General Conference Corporation of Seventh-day Adventists&rdquo;</strong> &mdash; a new organization.
        The storm and tempest <em>did</em> sweep away the structure. What exists today under that corporate name
        is not the church built by the Advent pioneers. It is the prophesied image.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- THE THREE ANGELS FRAMEWORK -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow">Revelation 14:6&ndash;12 &mdash; The Foundation</div>
      <h2>The Three Angels&rsquo; Messages:<br><em>The Framework for the Final Test</em></h2>
      <p class="sect-sub">You cannot understand what is happening in 2026 without understanding the Three Angels. They are not distant future prophecy. They frame <strong>exactly the situation we are living in right now.</strong></p>

      <div class="angels-grid">
        <div class="angel-card first">
          <div class="angel-header">
            <div class="angel-num num-gold">1st</div>
            <div class="angel-title">The Judgment Hour</div>
          </div>
          <div class="angel-ref-label">Revelation 14:6&ndash;7</div>
          <p class="angel-verse">&ldquo;Fear God, and give glory to him; for the hour of his judgment is come: and worship him that made heaven, and earth, and the sea.&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="angel-body">The judgment hour began in 1844. The Fourth Commandment &mdash; <strong>Remember the Sabbath day</strong> &mdash; is the seal of the Creator in that judgment. To fear God and worship Him as Creator IS to keep His Sabbath.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-card second">
          <div class="angel-header">
            <div class="angel-num num-red">2nd</div>
            <div class="angel-title">Babylon Is Fallen</div>
          </div>
          <div class="angel-ref-label">Revelation 14:8</div>
          <p class="angel-verse">&ldquo;Babylon is fallen, is fallen, that great city, because she made all nations drink of the wine of the wrath of her fornication.&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="angel-body">The Protestant churches fell in 1844 by rejecting the First Angel. Their falling did not stop &mdash; it accelerated. By 1904, <strong>even the Adventist corporate structure</strong> had replicated the papal union of church and state that Babylon defined.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-card third">
          <div class="angel-header">
            <div class="angel-num num-teal">3rd</div>
            <div class="angel-title">The Final Warning</div>
          </div>
          <div class="angel-ref-label">Revelation 14:9&ndash;12</div>
          <p class="angel-verse">&ldquo;If any man worship the beast and his image &hellip; Here are they that keep the commandments of God, and the faith of Jesus.&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="angel-body">The seal of God is the <strong>Seventh-day Sabbath</strong> &mdash; the sign of God&rsquo;s creative and redemptive authority. The mark of the beast is Sunday sacredness enforced in place of the Sabbath. <strong>There is no middle ground.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="banner-gold" style="margin-top:30px;">
        <div class="banner-gold-label">Ellen G. White &mdash; Selected Messages, Book 2, p. 104 (Manuscript 32, 1896)</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;The first and second messages were given in 1843 and 1844, and we are now under the proclamation of the third; but all three of the messages are still to be proclaimed. It is just as essential now as ever before that they shall be repeated to those who are seeking for the truth. By pen and voice we are to sound the proclamation, showing their order, and the application of the prophecies that bring us to the third angel&rsquo;s message. There cannot be a third without the first and second. These messages we are to give to the world in publications, in discourses, showing in the line of prophetic history the things that have been and the things that will be.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Ellen G. White &bull; Selected Messages, Book 2, p. 104 (Manuscript 32, 1896)</cite>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- WHAT IS THE IMAGE OF THE BEAST -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow-red">Revelation 13:14&ndash;15 &mdash; The Image Formed</div>
      <h2>What Is <em>The Image of the Beast?</em><br>It Is Already Formed &mdash; April 15, 1904</h2>

      <p class="sect-sub">
        The image of the beast is not a statue. It is not a microchip. <strong>It is a system.</strong>
        When a Protestant church submits itself to civil incorporation &mdash; when it registers under the authority of the state,
        grants the state governance over its legal structure, and becomes a creature of civil law &mdash; it has made
        <em>an exact image of the Papacy:</em> civil authority over religious life. That is the union of church and state.
        That is the beast&rsquo;s image. <strong>And the Adventist corporate body made that image on April 15, 1904.</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="def-grid">
        <div class="def-card papal">
          <h3>The Original Papacy (Rome)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Church rule enforced through the civil sword</li>
            <li>State punishes religious dissent as heresy</li>
            <li>Sunday sacredness mandated by law</li>
            <li>Dissenters fined, jailed, tortured, killed</li>
            <li>No separation between church authority and civil law</li>
            <li>Those who keep God&rsquo;s Sabbath are marked as criminals</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="def-card american">
          <h3>The Image &mdash; Corporate Adventism, 1904</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Church incorporated under the District of Columbia civil code</li>
            <li>501(c)(3) status: the state now governs the org&rsquo;s legal existence</li>
            <li>The corporation holds property, controls access to worship space</li>
            <li>Reformers expelled from church using state-backed corporate law</li>
            <li>Tithe pooled into corporate funds invested in Sunday commerce</li>
            <li>The form of godliness without the power (2 Tim. 3:5)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="banner-red">
        <div class="banner-red-label">Revelation 13:15 (KJV) &mdash; The Decree of the Image</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;And he had power to give life unto the image of the beast, that the image of the beast should both speak, and <strong>cause that as many as would not worship the image of the beast should be killed.</strong>&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Revelation 13:15 &mdash; The image speaks. It has the power of life and death over dissenters. This is the model the 1904 corporate structure put in place.</cite>
      </div>

      <div class="banner-gold">
        <div class="banner-gold-label">Ellen G. White &mdash; Testimonies to Ministers, p. 39</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;The image of the papacy is a combination of religious and civil power which shall say to those who will not subscribe to its edicts, <strong>&lsquo;You shall not buy or sell, and you shall suffer the severest penalties that our united power can inflict.&rsquo;</strong>&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Ellen G. White &mdash; Testimonies to Ministers and Gospel Workers, p. 39</cite>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- APRIL 15 1904 — THE FIVE SIGNERS -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow-red">April 15, 1904 &mdash; Washington, District of Columbia</div>
      <h2>The Day Five Men <em>Signed Away the Church</em><br>and Called It Organization</h2>

      <p class="sect-sub">
        On April 15, 1904 &mdash; precisely <strong>six months after Ellen White warned that entering any new organization would mean apostasy from the truth</strong> &mdash; five men sat down in Washington, District of Columbia and signed the Articles of Incorporation for the <em>&ldquo;General Conference Corporation of Seventh-day Adventists.&rdquo;</em>
        They created a legal corporation. They handed the church to the state. They built their foundation on the sand that EGW said the storm and tempest would sweep away.
        <strong>These are the five men who signed:</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="signers-strip">
        <a href="/1904-signers/james-r-scott" class="signer-mini">
          <div class="signer-mini-num">Signer 1</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-name">James R. Scott</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-role">Washington, D.C.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/1904-signers/harvey-edson-rogers" class="signer-mini">
          <div class="signer-mini-num">Signer 2</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-name">Harvey Edson Rogers</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-role">Washington, D.C.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/1904-signers/daniel-k-nicola" class="signer-mini">
          <div class="signer-mini-num">Signer 3</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-name">Daniel K. Nicola</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-role">Washington, D.C.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/1904-signers/arthur-g-daniells" class="signer-mini">
          <div class="signer-mini-num">Signer 4</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-name">Arthur G. Daniells</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-role">GC President, 1901&ndash;1922</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/1904-signers/amos-p-needham" class="signer-mini">
          <div class="signer-mini-num">Signer 5</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-name">Amos P. Needham</div>
          <div class="signer-mini-role">Washington, D.C.</div>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="sect-sub" style="margin-top:24px;">
        Every member of the SDA denomination today is a member of the legal successor to the corporation those five men created.
        Every building the church occupies, every publishing house, every hospital, every school &mdash; legally owned by
        the descendant of that 1904 corporation. When you sit in an SDA pew, <strong>you are sitting inside a 501(c)(3)
        state-controlled organization whose legal existence traces directly to April 15, 1904</strong> &mdash; the day EGW said was apostasy.
      </p>

      <div class="banner-gold">
        <div class="banner-gold-label">1905 Seventh-day Adventist Yearbook &mdash; The Primary Document</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;The name of the corporation hereby created shall be &lsquo;<strong>General Conference Corporation of Seventh-day Adventists.</strong>&rsquo; &hellip; The signers hereof, at Washington, in the District of Columbia, this <strong>fifteenth day of April, A.D. 1904.</strong>&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; 1905 SDA Yearbook &mdash; Articles of Incorporation &mdash; The Primary Source &mdash;
          <a href="/books/1904-image-of-papacy/seventh-day-adventist-yearbook-1905.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--gold-soft);text-decoration:underline;">Open PDF &rarr;</a>
        </cite>
      </div>

      <div class="v-timeline">
        <div class="vt-item">
          <div class="vt-dot gold">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="vt-content">
            <div class="vt-year">Letter 242, September 1903</div>
            <div class="vt-title">EGW Issues the Warning</div>
            <div class="vt-body">Ellen White writes to General Conference leaders: <strong>&ldquo;We cannot now enter into any new organization; for this would mean apostasy from the truth.&rdquo;</strong> The warning could not be clearer. It is ignored.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
