    <!-- THE MAYFLOWER — SAME TYRANNY, DIFFERENT CENTURY -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow">1620 &mdash; 1904 &mdash; 2026 &mdash; Same Persecutor, Different Clothes</div>
      <h2>The Mayflower Fled <em>Exactly This.</em><br>And Now It Has Come Back.</h2>

      <div class="mayflower-grid">
        <div class="mayflower-img-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/sundaylaw/mayflower-1620-religious-freedom-james-white-family-escaping-state-church-tyranny-sundaylaw.jpg"
            alt="The Mayflower, 1620 &mdash; Fleeing Religious Tyranny of the State Church"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="mayflower-img-label">The Mayflower, 1620 &mdash; Fleeing the Church of England&rsquo;s Persecuting Arm</div>
        </div>

        <div class="mayflower-content">
          <h3>From Plymouth Rock to Washington, D.C.:<br>The Circle of Tyranny Closes</h3>
          <p>
            In <strong>1620</strong>, the Pilgrims jammed themselves into a tiny vessel called the Mayflower and left everything they knew to cross a violent winter ocean. What were they fleeing? <em>Exactly what you are being asked to submit to right now.</em>
            They were fleeing the <strong>Church of England</strong> &mdash; a state church, incorporated under the crown, that used civil law to compel religious conformity. Worship the king&rsquo;s way. Observe the king&rsquo;s Sunday. Submit to the king&rsquo;s sacraments. Or be fined, jailed, silenced, destroyed.
          </p>
          <p>
            They crossed the ocean for one reason: <strong>so that no government, no king, and no incorporated church could dictate their conscience before God.</strong>
            They wrote the First Amendment to guarantee that their sacrifice would not be undone.
          </p>
          <p>
            And on <strong>April 15, 1904</strong>, in the capital city of the nation they built, five men quietly undid it.
            They incorporated the Adventist body into the very system the Pilgrims had bled to escape.
            Not by violence. By paperwork. By a corporate charter filed in Washington, D.C.
            <em>The new organization was the old tyranny reborn.</em>
          </p>
          <div class="warn-box">
            &#9888;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Church of England used Sunday law to enforce religious conformity. The 501(c)(3) corporate church uses tax exemption, property ownership, and credentialing to enforce conformity today. The method changed. <strong>The spirit of Babylon did not.</strong> &ldquo;Come out of her, my people&rdquo; (Rev. 18:4) is addressed to <em>you</em> &mdash; right now &mdash; in 2026.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="banner-blue">
        <div class="banner-blue-label">First Amendment &mdash; United States Constitution, December 15, 1791</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;Congress shall make no law respecting an establishment of religion, or prohibiting the free exercise thereof; or abridging the freedom of speech, or of the press; or the right of the people peaceably to assemble, and to petition the Government for a redress of grievances.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; The First Amendment &mdash; written specifically to prevent what the Church of England did &mdash; and what the 1904 SDA Corporation quietly reversed</cite>
      </div>

      <div class="banner-gold">
        <div class="banner-gold-label">Alonzo T. Jones &mdash; The Two Republics, 1891</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;The Reformers protested against the union of church and state. But the children of the Reformers have returned to Egypt. They build what their fathers pulled down. Heaven marks the movement: it is the image of the beast.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Alonzo T. Jones &mdash; religious liberty pioneer, Adventist minister, 1891 &mdash; written 13 years before April 15, 1904</cite>
      </div>

      <div class="banner-red" style="margin-top:28px;">
        <div class="banner-red-label">Ellen G. White &mdash; 1888 Materials, p. 356.4 &bull; Ms. 30, 1889 &mdash; Written After Minneapolis</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;I was confirmed in all I had stated in Minneapolis, that a reformation must go through the churches. Reforms must be made, for spiritual weakness and blindness were upon the people who had been blessed with great light and precious opportunities and privileges. As reformers they had come out of the denominational churches, but they now act a part similar to that which the churches acted. <strong>We hoped that there would not be the necessity for another coming out.</strong> While we will endeavor to keep the &lsquo;unity of the Spirit&rsquo; in the bonds of peace, we will not with pen or voice cease to protest against bigotry.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Ellen G. White &bull; 1888 Materials, p. 356.4 &bull; Ms. 30, 1889 &mdash; Written 15 years before 1904 &mdash; She hoped there would be no &ldquo;another coming out.&rdquo; There was.</cite>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 501(C)(3) — THE STATE CHURCH TODAY — SHOCKING -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow-red">&#9888; Religious Tyranny in Tax-Exempt Clothing &mdash; The Truth They Do Not Want You to Know</div>
      <h2>The 501(c)(3) Church Is<br><em>A State-Controlled Institution.</em><br>This Is Not a Metaphor.</h2>

      <p class="sect-sub">
        When the Pilgrim Fathers fled the Church of England, the weapon used against them was <em>legal incorporation.</em>
        A church under a crown charter was a legal body <strong>subject to the king&rsquo;s law,</strong> not God&rsquo;s law alone.
        When the king said Sunday, it said Sunday. When the crown said silence the dissenter, it silenced them.
        A 501(c)(3) organization is the direct American equivalent.
        It is a <strong>federally recognized legal entity</strong> operating under a contract with the United States government
        that dictates what it may and may not say, who it must legally serve, and how it must structure its governance.
        <em>The IRS is the landlord. The congregation is a tenant.</em>
        <strong>That is the image of the beast. It is not forming. It formed in 1904. You are inside it right now.</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="expose-card">
        <h3>What Your 501(c)(3) Church Is Actually Forbidden to Do &mdash; By Law, By IRS Contract</h3>
        <ul class="expose-list">
          <li><strong>Cannot endorse or oppose any candidate for political office</strong> &mdash; meaning your pastor cannot expose a politician who pushes Sunday laws without jeopardizing the church&rsquo;s tax status. The very warning the Third Angel calls for is legally gagged.</li>
          <li><strong>Cannot take substantial lobbying positions on legislation</strong> &mdash; meaning the church that was built to warn against Sunday law legislation cannot substantially advocate against it without risking IRS discipline.</li>
          <li><strong>Must file IRS Form 990 or lose tax exemption</strong> &mdash; disclosing finances, governance structure, and key employees to the federal government. The state knows your church&rsquo;s every financial move.</li>
          <li><strong>All property held in the corporate name is property of the corporation,</strong> not the members. If you are expelled, the building remains with the corporation. This is the landlord-tenant relationship &mdash; the civil arm controls access to worship space.</li>
          <li><strong>The corporation&rsquo;s legal charter supersedes congregational authority</strong> on structural matters. The board of directors, not the biblical eldership, holds legal power. The state created those structures in 1904.</li>
          <li><strong>Donors receive tax deductions for tithes and offerings</strong> &mdash; making every tithe dollar a joint financial arrangement with the federal government. Your offering has been co-signed by the IRS.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="sect-sub">
        <strong>This is not a conspiracy theory. This is contract law.</strong>
        The SDA denomination entered this contract voluntarily on April 15, 1904 and has renewed it every year since
        through continuing 501(c)(3) registration. The Pilgrims shivered aboard a leaking ship crossing the North Atlantic
        to escape this exact arrangement. Their descendants are paying tithe into the heart of it.
        <strong>Heaven marks the movement. And the Loud Cry is calling you OUT.</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="banner-red">
        <div class="banner-red-label">James White &mdash; Review &amp; Herald, 1877 &mdash; The Warning</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;The two-horned beast is the United States of America &mdash; &lsquo;two horns like a lamb&rsquo; &mdash; the civil and religious powers of the republic. But when the image is formed &mdash; that is, when a church uses the civil arm to enforce its decrees &mdash; then these lamb-like horns <strong>&lsquo;speak as a dragon.&rsquo;</strong>&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; James White &mdash; Review &amp; Herald, 1877 &mdash; 27 years before April 15, 1904</cite>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- THE LOUD CRY — REVELATION 18 -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow-red">Revelation 18:1&ndash;5 &mdash; The Loudest Voice in Scripture</div>
      <h2>The Loud Cry Is Sounding.<br><em>Come Out of Her, My People &mdash; NOW.</em></h2>

      <div class="loud-cry-banner">
        <h3>The Angel With Great Power &mdash; The Earth Lightened With His Glory</h3>

        <div class="loud-cry-verse">
          <div class="loud-cry-ref">Revelation 18:1&ndash;2 (KJV) &mdash; The Loud Cry Angel</div>
          <blockquote>
            &ldquo;And after these things I saw another angel come down from heaven, having great power; and the earth was lightened with his glory. And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying, <strong>Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen,</strong> and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird.&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          <cite>&mdash; Revelation 18:1&ndash;2 (KJV)</cite>
        </div>

        <div class="loud-cry-verse" style="margin-top:14px;">
          <div class="loud-cry-ref">Revelation 18:4&ndash;5 (KJV) &mdash; The Voice From Heaven &mdash; YOUR Personal Call</div>
          <blockquote>
            &ldquo;And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, <strong>Come out of her, my people,</strong> that ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues. For her sins have reached unto heaven, and God hath remembered her iniquities.&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          <cite>&mdash; Revelation 18:4&ndash;5 (KJV) &mdash; The command is not optional. It is not conditional. It is addressed to <em>MY PEOPLE</em> &mdash; people who are currently INSIDE Babylon.</cite>
        </div>

        <p>
          Notice who this command is addressed to: <strong>&ldquo;my people.&rdquo;</strong> Not the heathen. Not the atheist. Not the Sunday-keeping world.
          This voice calls to people who belong to God, who love God, who are inside a religious institution &mdash;
          <em>and who are standing inside Babylon right now without knowing it.</em>
          The call is personal, urgent, and final: <strong>Come out. Before you partake of her plagues.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          The plagues of Revelation 16 fall on Babylon specifically because of her union with the state, her enforcement of false worship, and her persecution of those who keep the commandments of God.
          If you remain inside the 501(c)(3) incorporated SDA corporate structure when those plagues fall,
          you have chosen your side in the final conflict.
          <strong>Your eternal destiny is decided by this choice.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="banner-gold">
        <div class="banner-gold-label">Ellen G. White &mdash; Great Controversy, p. 606</div>
        <blockquote>&ldquo;The message of the fall of Babylon, as given by the second angel, is repeated, with the additional mention of the corruptions which have been entering the churches since 1844. The work of this angel comes in at the right time to join in the last great work of the third angel&rsquo;s message as it swells to a loud cry.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>&mdash; Ellen G. White &mdash; The Great Controversy, p. 606 &mdash; The Loud Cry amplifies the Second Angel with the weight of every corruption since 1844, including 1904</cite>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- YOUR RESPONSE — STEPS -->
    <div class="sect">
      <div class="sect-eyebrow">Practical Obedience &mdash; What Does &ldquo;Come Out&rdquo; Actually Mean?</div>
      <h2>The Test Is Not Theoretical.<br><em>Here Is What Obedience Looks Like.</em></h2>

      <p class="sect-sub">
        The test that decides your eternal destiny is not a theology exam.
        It is not a committee vote. It is not a denominational transfer form.
        <strong>It is personal obedience to God&rsquo;s word at great personal cost,</strong>
        in the face of family pressure, social pressure, financial pressure, and the weight of tradition.
        The Pilgrims did not flee England by committee. They obeyed God and got on the boat.
        Here is what the Loud Cry calls you to do:
      </p>

      <ul class="steps-list">
        <li>
          <div class="step-num">1</div>
          <div class="step-text"><strong>Read the primary documents.</strong> Do not take our word for it. Download the <em>1905 SDA Yearbook PDF</em> and read the Articles of Incorporation yourself. Read 1SM 204 in full context. Read Revelation 18 with fresh eyes. Verify every claim against the original sources.</div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="step-num">2</div>
          <div class="step-text"><strong>Understand what you are part of.</strong> Your local SDA church operates under authority that traces to the April 15, 1904 corporate charter. The building is owned by the corporation. The organization is registered as a 501(c)(3) federal tax-exempt entity. This is not opinion. This is legal public record.</div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="step-num">3</div>
          <div class="step-text"><strong>Ask the hard question: Is this the church the pioneers built?</strong> William Miller, Charles Fitch, Joseph Bates, James White, Hiram Edson &mdash; every one of them left their denomination when that denomination proved unfaithful. They did not leave God. They left <em>Babylon</em> &mdash; and found the present truth. <strong>The same call is sounding today.</strong></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="step-num">4</div>
          <div class="step-text"><strong>Keep all the commandments of God (Revelation 14:12).</strong> The Seventh-day Sabbath is the seal of the living God (Rev. 7:2&ndash;3, Ex. 20:8&ndash;11). The Fourth Commandment is not abolished. It is not replaced. It is the test commandment &mdash; the one that identifies whose worship you are offering: <em>the Creator&rsquo;s</em> or <em>the beast&rsquo;s.</em></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="step-num">5</div>
          <div class="step-text"><strong>Come out in faith &mdash; not in anger, but in obedience.</strong> The call of Revelation 18:4 is not a call to condemn individuals. It is a call to separate from a system. You can love people inside Babylon while refusing to remain in Babylon. Come out. Bring others with you. <strong>This is the patient endurance of the saints (Rev. 14:12).</strong></div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

